447: ## SCN.9. The C2 characteristic bordism has no outer mismatch
448: 
449: There is also a direct narrow repair of the integer
450: characteristic comparison. At the first fixed branch
451: of the \(C_2\) native star, its fixed base and normal
452: pair are exactly \(b\) and \((a,c)\). At the second,
453: they are \(w\) and \((v,u)\). Relative to the native
454: \(C_0\) coordinates (SCN.15), the second arrow is
455: \[
456:  \text{base factor }\kappa^{-1},\qquad
457:  \text{normal matrix }\operatorname{diag}
458:                            (\alpha^{-1},\kappa\alpha).
459:                                                         \tag{SCN.27}
460: \]
461: Both this map and its first-branch identity are
462: independent of the scalar parameter. After carrying
463: their fixed logarithms, the outer normal maps are
464: constant in that parameter.
465: 
466: In the \(C_2\) Cox coordinates of (SCN.23), the
467: parameter factor has physical weights
468: \((0,-1,0,+1)\). The two inner charged boundary maps
469: therefore have one identical scalar gauge, as in
470: the actual master and joint-cap maps of K17.
471: Use that same scalar on every Cox chart and on the
472: joint cap. It commutes with their actual transition
473: functions. The outer identifications (SCN.27) are
474: constant in the parameter, so this gauge matches
475: the two outer conifold products as well. Unlike
476: SCN.17, there is no endpoint-dependent parameter
477: transition left on the fixed-cobordism closure.
478: 
479: The line on the closed five-dimensional orbit
480: correction is consequently the pullback of its
481: parameter-zero line. The same is true of its
482: tangent bundle under the literal moment-chart
483: maps and constant bounded-unit isotopies. Its
484: six-dimensional numbers \(x^3,p_1x\) vanish.
485: On the additional normal-sphere boundary the
486: closed four-dimensional fixed base is the
487: oriented \(S^2\) mapping torus crossed with the
488: parameter circle, with all its normal and line
489: transitions pulled back from the three-dimensional
490: factor. Thus its actual class \(b\) has \(b^2=0\),
491: and the base tangent Pontryagin number is zero.
492: The sphere-bundle identity
493: \[
494:        \frac{4\int x^3-\int p_1x}{24}
495:                  =\frac{3\int b^2-\int p_1(T\bar X)}{24}
496: \]
497: gives zero for this retained boundary. This proves
498: equality of the two integer characteristic indices
499: for this particular \(C_2\) comparison. It proves
500: no equality for the \(C_1\) comparison, whose
501: actual outer map is (SCN.17).
